      "Does an apparently completed outsourced item create repair work in another team, channel, or reporting period? Define the eligible population as eligible completed outsourced items and linked downstream records during a declared follow-up window. The observation unit is one completed item linked to source, output, review, destination, downstream correction, repair owner, effort state, and accepted final state. Freeze purpose, period, systems, service windows, owners, inclusion rules, and exclusions before viewing results. Philippines-based analysts may assemble protected evidence, apply a codebook, calculate declared measures, and flag conflicts. Accountable company owners retain policy, pricing, money, employment, legal, security, safety, customer commitments, and risk acceptance. The protocol evaluates a local operating process; it does not certify a provider, rank a worker, establish a universal benchmark, or guarantee an outcome. For Downstream Rework Discoverability Between Outsourced and Internal Teams, analysis checkpoint 1 preserves its eligible denominator, missing-evidence count, adverse case, owner disposition, and the boundary between operational observation and consequential decision.",
